      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "Use of proceeds We will not receive any of the\n                                            proceeds from the resale of the Purchase Shares by Roth Principal Investments. However, we\n                                            may receive up to $25,000,000 in aggregate gross proceeds under the Purchase Agreement from\n                                            any sales of Purchase Shares we make to Roth Principal Investments pursuant to the Purchase\n                                            Agreement, assuming that we sell the full amount of our Class A ordinary shares that we have\n                                            the right, but not the obligation, to sell to Roth Principal Investments under the Purchase\n                                            Agreement. Any proceeds that we receive from sales of Class A ordinary shares to Roth Principal\n                                 ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION While secondary sales of the Class\u00a0A\nordinary shares by the Selling Shareholder will not have a dilutive effect on our shareholders, the issuance of Class A ordinary shares\nto the Selling Shareholder pursuant to the Purchase Agreement will have a dilutive impact on shareholders. Dilution\nresults from the fact that the per share offering price of the Class\u00a0A ordinary shares is substantially in excess of the net\ntangible book value attributable to the existing shareholders. Net tangible book value represents the amount of our total assets\nless our total liabilities, excluding goodwill and other intangible assets. Net tangible book value per Class A ordinary share\nrepresents net tangible book value attributable to Class A ordinary shares divided by 11,717,133, the total number of our Class A\nordinary shares outstanding as of the date of this prospectus. As of June 30, 2026, we had ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
